# RiceSearcher — local secrets/config (example).
#
# Copy to `credentials.env` (gitignored) and fill in. RiceSearcher loads
# `credentials.env` (then `.env`) from the current directory before running a
# command; an explicit shell `export` always wins over these files.

# Anthropic API key — used ONLY by the scorer (`ricesearcher score`). Nothing
# else in this project calls a paid API. Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/
# Uncomment and paste your real key. Left as the placeholder, `score` would send
# it and fail with a 401 authentication_error.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional: override the scorer model (default: claude-haiku-5-5, the lowest-cost
# option). Set a more capable/pricier model here if wanted.
# RICESEARCHER_SCORER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# Beat profiles are chosen per command with `--profile ID`; there is no env var
# for them (RICESEARCHER_BEAT_PROFILE was retired by ADR-002).

# Optional: sentence-transformers model used by `dedup` (default: all-MiniLM-L6-v2).
# RICESEARCHER_EMBED_MODEL=all-MiniLM-L6-v2

# Data paths: leave these unset. Unset, they are what `rice data location`
# reports, the same paths `rice start` uses. A value here wins exactly like a
# shell export, but `rice start` never reads this file, so pinning an old path
# (e.g. ~/.ricesearcher after `rice data cutover`) splits the standalone CLI
# from the suite. Set them only for a disposable trial.

# Optional: local data root (library, media cache, profiles).
# RICESEARCHER_DATA_DIR=/tmp/rs-trial/data

# Optional: override where beat-profile JSON files live (default:
# <data_dir>/profiles, or ricesuite.env's RICESEARCHER_PROFILES_DIR).
# RICESEARCHER_PROFILES_DIR=/tmp/rs-trial/profiles

# Optional: RiceSearcher's own handoff root that RiceClipper pulls from. NOT
# ~/riceclipper-handoff (that's RiceClipper's output to RicePoster). Must match
# RiceClipper's inbox setting.
# RICESEARCHER_HANDOFF_DIR=/tmp/rs-trial/handoff
